1
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:36,661
I'm just worried.

2
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:41,041
I know. I'm also worried.

3
00:00:57,724 --> 00:00:58,850
This can't be.

4
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:01,311
<i>The bomb.</i>

5
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:04,147
We can't let them get it.

6
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:08,568
I have a strong feeling
it shouldn't end up in their hands.

7
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:12,530
<i>We're all doomed</i>
<i>if the bomb falls into their hands.</i>

8
00:01:12,614 --> 00:01:13,573
We are going to die.

9
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:16,618
In case we can't make sure
that both of them are safe,

10
00:01:16,701 --> 00:01:17,994
we are also risking their lives.

11
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:26,127
Split up!

12
00:01:26,836 --> 00:01:28,046
You go over there. We'll go this way.

13
00:01:28,129 --> 00:01:30,465
Well? Did you see them?

14
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:31,633
Let's go, let's go!

15
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:36,513
- Don't make a sound.
- Lady Amor?

16
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:38,765
Follow me. Hurry!

17
00:01:38,848 --> 00:01:41,392
Let's go, Angelito. Let's go, let's go.

18
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:43,686
- Move.
- Okay.

19
00:02:35,738 --> 00:02:37,115
Try it again.

20
00:02:58,386 --> 00:02:59,220
I'm out of ammo.

21
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:00,638
Me too.

22
00:03:33,755 --> 00:03:34,923
Let's go!

23
00:04:15,505 --> 00:04:16,589
Sianong!

24
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:29,894
Sianong!

25
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:33,481
- Come on.
- Let's go.

26
00:04:34,190 --> 00:04:35,024
‪Let's go.

27
00:04:40,113 --> 00:04:41,447
Just a little more.

28
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:44,784
‪Hey.

29
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:45,952
Hurry up.

30
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:49,247
We're almost there.

31
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:50,498
Come on.

32
00:04:50,581 --> 00:04:51,791
Just a little farther.

33
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:55,420
You can do it.

34
00:05:03,511 --> 00:05:06,347
Come inside. We're here.

35
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:09,183
Have a seat first.

36
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:10,643
Easy, Angelito.

37
00:05:13,479 --> 00:05:16,190
I'll get you some water to drink.

38
00:05:16,899 --> 00:05:18,401
Are you okay, Angelito?

39
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:23,906
Drink some water first, Angelito.

40
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:25,033
Thank you.

41
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:41,591
Sianong.

42
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:43,342
Agent Sean Salindong.

43
00:05:43,426 --> 00:05:44,510
Don't fall asleep.

44
00:05:45,553 --> 00:05:46,721
I'm not sleeping.

45
00:05:46,804 --> 00:05:48,389
- I'm just resting.
- Okay.

46
00:05:48,473 --> 00:05:50,767
Wait. Hold on.

47
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:53,144
For the record.

48
00:05:53,227 --> 00:05:55,730
Chiara. I'm not a traitor.

49
00:05:55,813 --> 00:05:58,858
Whatever you heard, it was just gossip.

50
00:06:08,326 --> 00:06:10,495
Come on, after everything
we've been through.

51
00:06:10,578 --> 00:06:12,205
You even side-kicked me earlier.

52
00:06:12,288 --> 00:06:14,665
Want me to side-kick you again?

53
00:06:24,717 --> 00:06:25,760
What's that?

54
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:39,816
Wake up, wake up.

55
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:49,992
Let's go over there.

56
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:51,786
- Come on.
- Are you okay?

57
00:06:57,792 --> 00:06:59,585
The T-Rex must leave.

58
00:07:38,499 --> 00:07:40,209
Come on, this way.

59
00:07:51,095 --> 00:07:52,096
Oh my gosh.

60
00:07:55,016 --> 00:07:57,059
I'll report to Sir Norberto.

61
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:14,785
- With whom?
- All three.

62
00:09:12,051 --> 00:09:14,095
Come on, eat.

63
00:09:14,178 --> 00:09:16,264
- Agent Alex.
- Yes, ma'am.

64
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:31,070
You're feeling down, aren't you?

65
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:33,614
You miss them.

66
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:38,035
Don't worry. They'll be back.

67
00:10:24,498 --> 00:10:26,626
Agent Alex, what does that mean?

68
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:27,710
Is it Mikoy and the others?

69
00:10:27,793 --> 00:10:29,754
What? Agent Alex, what is it?

70
00:10:30,588 --> 00:10:32,173
- What happened?
- Agent--

71
00:10:32,798 --> 00:10:33,883
Did they…

72
00:10:33,966 --> 00:10:35,926
Oh God…

73
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:45,770
Go ahead and eat, okay?

74
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:48,230
I still have something to do
in the kitchen.

75
00:10:48,314 --> 00:10:49,815
- Go on.
- Thank you.

76
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:50,983
Thank you.

77
00:10:55,696 --> 00:10:57,406
- This is all my fault.
- Thank you.

78
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:04,246
If only I hadn't insisted.

79
00:11:04,830 --> 00:11:07,917
If only I had listened to you.

80
00:11:08,417 --> 00:11:09,502
Then this wouldn't…

81
00:11:10,211 --> 00:11:11,879
It's not your fault.

82
00:11:13,381 --> 00:11:14,298
How is it not?

83
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:24,016
You weren't the one who brought
a whole bunch of armed men here.

84
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:27,353
But if only…

85
00:11:28,104 --> 00:11:32,108
I hadn't been so stubborn and impulsive.

86
00:11:32,608 --> 00:11:33,692
Then…

87
00:11:35,277 --> 00:11:37,571
maybe we'd still have been captured.

88
00:11:39,073 --> 00:11:40,241
We don't know.

89
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:44,745
We don't know.

90
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:48,833
That's why I'm sorry.

91
00:11:51,585 --> 00:11:52,920
Are you okay?

92
00:11:53,003 --> 00:11:54,213
Are you hurt?

93
00:11:56,298 --> 00:11:57,174
I'm okay.

94
00:11:59,218 --> 00:12:02,763
I actually got a rush of adrenaline
when we ran.

95
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:09,979
Whatever happens, I'll take care of you.

96
00:12:10,813 --> 00:12:12,481
I'll never leave you.

97
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:17,528
Go on, eat.

98
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:20,781
So you'll have the energy.

99
00:12:43,387 --> 00:12:44,805
I'll take care of this.

100
00:12:47,558 --> 00:12:49,518
Agent Alex, take this for the road.

101
00:12:50,102 --> 00:12:51,896
Thank you, Tess.

102
00:12:51,979 --> 00:12:53,898
Agent Alex. Come back soon, okay?

103
00:12:54,398 --> 00:12:55,483
We won't have anyone to tease.

104
00:12:55,566 --> 00:12:57,735
And no one to panic.

105
00:12:57,818 --> 00:12:59,320
Or get annoyed.

106
00:12:59,403 --> 00:13:01,280
Yes, and we won't have anyone
to play charades with.

107
00:13:01,363 --> 00:13:04,116
The one who makes us guess "elephant".

108
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,117
Stuff like that.

109
00:13:05,993 --> 00:13:07,286
That's enough.

110
00:13:07,369 --> 00:13:09,955
We all know Agent Alex will be back soon.

111
00:13:10,039 --> 00:13:13,209
She can't stay away from me for too long.

112
00:13:14,543 --> 00:13:15,711
Alex.

113
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:17,087
Come back soon, okay?

114
00:13:17,171 --> 00:13:18,464
For us.

115
00:13:20,799 --> 00:13:21,634
You jerk!

116
00:13:23,719 --> 00:13:27,973
Don't come back if it's just for him.

117
00:13:28,057 --> 00:13:30,142
Ouch, Tess!

118
00:13:35,648 --> 00:13:36,607
Like you've got a fever.

119
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:41,654
What do you call Sir Ben when he's sick?

120
00:13:41,737 --> 00:13:43,280
What do you call him?

121
00:13:43,364 --> 00:13:44,281
- What?
- What?

122
00:13:47,451 --> 00:13:49,078
Sick-si-Ben.

123
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:51,247
- Sick-si-Ben?
- Sick-si-Ben.

124
00:13:52,164 --> 00:13:52,998
Sick-si-Ben.

125
00:13:53,582 --> 00:13:54,500
Sick-si-Ben.

126
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:55,876
Sick-si-Ben.

127
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,503
Sick-si-Ben.

128
00:13:58,003 --> 00:13:59,004
Sick-si-Ben.

129
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:00,297
Sick-si-Ben.

130
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:01,632
- All right, I'll get going.
- All right.

131
00:14:02,216 --> 00:14:03,968
- We'll miss you.
- Sick-si-Ben.

132
00:14:04,051 --> 00:14:05,427
- Take care.
- Take care, sir.

133
00:14:05,511 --> 00:14:07,096
Sick-si-Ben.

134
00:14:07,179 --> 00:14:08,681
Sick-si-Ben.

135
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:09,932
Sick-si-Ben.

136
00:14:10,015 --> 00:14:11,183
Sick-si-Ben.

137
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:17,481
- Come on, hurry!
- Hang in there, Sianong.

138
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:18,983
We're at the vehicle.

139
00:14:19,942 --> 00:14:20,776
Come on.

140
00:14:22,027 --> 00:14:24,280
Hey, don't fall asleep.
We're almost there.

141
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:25,990
- Here we are.
- Quick, over here.

142
00:14:26,073 --> 00:14:26,907
Come on.

143
00:14:28,534 --> 00:14:29,869
Here we go, here we go.

144
00:14:29,952 --> 00:14:30,870
All right, lie down.

145
00:14:31,453 --> 00:14:32,746
- Wait.
- Easy, easy.

146
00:14:35,916 --> 00:14:36,792
Easy.

147
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:43,007
Seriously? I'm a person, not a sack!

148
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:46,343
I'm just used to carrying rice sacks.

149
00:15:02,192 --> 00:15:03,485
Oh, right.

150
00:15:04,153 --> 00:15:05,154
Brusko.

151
00:15:06,405 --> 00:15:07,448
Mikoy?

152
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:17,583
By the way, I'm Brusko.

153
00:15:26,258 --> 00:15:27,217
Hold on tight, okay?

154
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:28,344
Hang on.

155
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:30,596
Stay right there.

156
00:15:37,686 --> 00:15:38,896
How are you?

157
00:15:41,523 --> 00:15:42,816
Still alive.

158
00:15:43,817 --> 00:15:44,818
Seriously?

159
00:15:44,902 --> 00:15:48,238
I got shot in the shoulder.

160
00:15:48,322 --> 00:15:49,865
It's just a flesh wound.

161
00:15:50,574 --> 00:15:51,533
Chiara, what's that?

162
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:55,204
What's that?

163
00:15:55,287 --> 00:15:56,330
Ow!

164
00:16:01,752 --> 00:16:03,837
You don't need surgery right away.

165
00:16:14,765 --> 00:16:15,766
There isn't any.

166
00:16:17,726 --> 00:16:18,811
Really?

167
00:16:18,894 --> 00:16:20,688
Why? Were you hoping there was?

168
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:22,982
Nothing.

169
00:16:24,066 --> 00:16:27,152
You know, it just

170
00:16:28,112 --> 00:16:31,699
reminded me of something about Agent Alex.

171
00:16:33,409 --> 00:16:34,076
What?

172
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,705
One early morning,

173
00:16:39,081 --> 00:16:42,626
around three o'clock, it was quiet.

174
00:16:43,627 --> 00:16:45,087
Everyone was asleep.

175
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:47,798
I saw her in the dining area.

176
00:16:56,265 --> 00:16:58,851
<i>As if she was writing something important.</i>

177
00:17:02,646 --> 00:17:03,772
Alex?

178
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:10,571
<i>Writing?</i>

179
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:12,489
What was she writing?

180
00:17:13,365 --> 00:17:15,284
That's exactly why I got curious.

181
00:17:15,367 --> 00:17:19,496
Even I know she absolutely hates
writing by hand.

182
00:17:19,580 --> 00:17:23,292
Besides, she's kind of awkward
when it comes to handwriting.

183
00:17:23,876 --> 00:17:26,086
So I walked over to her.

184
00:17:26,795 --> 00:17:27,671
<i>I asked…</i>

185
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:29,173
What are you doing?

186
00:17:29,256 --> 00:17:30,257
<i>She said…</i>

187
00:17:31,341 --> 00:17:34,470
I'm… I'm practicing.

188
00:17:35,637 --> 00:17:37,056
Practicing what?

189
00:17:37,931 --> 00:17:40,100
My…

190
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:41,060
penmanship.

191
00:17:41,685 --> 00:17:43,562
- Penmanship?
- Yes.

192
00:17:45,689 --> 00:17:47,399
At three in the morning?

193
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:48,942
Yes, that's ridiculous.

194
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:50,402
Practicing penmanship at 3 a.m.

195
00:17:50,486 --> 00:17:52,529
I don't buy it, Chiara.

196
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:53,906
Neither do I.

197
00:17:54,406 --> 00:17:55,908
So I got even closer.

198
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:10,506
<i>I think I saw something on the paper.</i>

199
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:13,217
<i>"Sia…"</i>

200
00:18:15,886 --> 00:18:17,596
What happened? "Sia"?

201
00:18:17,679 --> 00:18:19,431
What happened? What came next?

202
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:21,975
I don't know.
I didn't see the whole thing.

203
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:24,853
But… Who knows?

204
00:18:24,937 --> 00:18:26,772
Maybe "Sia" stands for…

205
00:18:26,855 --> 00:18:28,398
Siargao.

206
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:36,657
Why would Alex be writing
a Siargao itinerary?

207
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:37,825
She doesn't even like the beach.

208
00:18:38,408 --> 00:18:39,910
She's so fair-skinned.

209
00:18:39,993 --> 00:18:42,538
She could've just used Google Sheets.

210
00:18:42,621 --> 00:18:43,622
- Exactly.
- Right?

211
00:18:43,705 --> 00:18:44,414
Yes.

212
00:18:45,082 --> 00:18:47,334
That note… The note?

213
00:18:47,417 --> 00:18:48,293
Where is it?

214
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:53,924
Well, I left.

215
00:18:54,007 --> 00:18:55,843
<i>But before I did…</i>

216
00:18:57,469 --> 00:18:59,096
<i>she looked at it again.</i>

217
00:18:59,596 --> 00:19:02,349
<i>Then she smiled.</i>

218
00:19:09,106 --> 00:19:10,023
Hey!

219
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:12,317
Hey!

220
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:15,279
Are you saying she has a crush?

221
00:19:15,362 --> 00:19:16,697
On Sianong?

222
00:19:17,364 --> 00:19:18,323
On Sianong?

223
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:20,159
- Hey.
- It's Sianong!

224
00:19:20,242 --> 00:19:21,535
Hey, hey!

225
00:19:21,618 --> 00:19:23,996
I'm getting butterflies!

226
00:19:29,459 --> 00:19:31,753
So… Where is it? Where's the paper?

227
00:19:31,837 --> 00:19:33,130
I want to see it.

228
00:19:33,213 --> 00:19:34,131
The paper?

229
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:36,091
- Yes, yes.
- Well…

230
00:19:36,175 --> 00:19:37,217
There wasn't one.

231
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:39,428
There!

232
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:48,228
Come on, Chiara.

233
00:19:48,312 --> 00:19:49,479
Why'd you do that?

234
00:19:49,563 --> 00:19:50,439
That hurt!

235
00:19:51,231 --> 00:19:52,441
What was that?

236
00:19:52,524 --> 00:19:53,567
A distraction.

237
00:19:54,151 --> 00:19:56,278
That whole story was just a distraction.

238
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:59,656
That really hurt.

239
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:01,742
All of it?

240
00:20:02,743 --> 00:20:04,912
Even the "Sia" part?

241
00:20:07,831 --> 00:20:09,082
Even the "Sia".

242
00:20:09,166 --> 00:20:10,751
Even the "Sia".

243
00:20:12,878 --> 00:20:13,837
But hey,

244
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:17,132
at least you didn't notice

245
00:20:17,633 --> 00:20:19,551
that the bullet
was already out of your back.

246
00:20:20,802 --> 00:20:23,847
Not bad. It worked. But that was harsh.

247
00:20:24,514 --> 00:20:25,682
What a shame.

248
00:20:25,766 --> 00:20:27,684
I almost believed you.

249
00:20:28,352 --> 00:20:30,729
You know, I know where she lives.

250
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:32,189
- Where?
- Q.C.

251
00:20:32,773 --> 00:20:34,608
- Why?
- "PAG-ASA", hope.

252
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:44,952
Siargao.

253
00:20:52,417 --> 00:20:54,002
"Sia…"

254
00:21:02,261 --> 00:21:03,720
Okay, you can get some rest now.

255
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:19,695
Sianong.

256
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:25,659
For what?

257
00:21:27,369 --> 00:21:28,954
For taking that bullet for me.

258
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:34,209
You didn't have to do that.

259
00:21:39,089 --> 00:21:40,507
You're making assumptions

260
00:21:41,591 --> 00:21:43,302
because what I did for you

261
00:21:43,927 --> 00:21:47,931
isn't the same as what Mikoy did for you.

262
00:21:50,684 --> 00:21:55,647
I did it because you're one of us now.

263
00:22:03,238 --> 00:22:04,656
- Finally!
- It finally sparked!

264
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:08,910
Oh, right. Sorry. Yes!

265
00:22:28,263 --> 00:22:31,850
RADIOACTIVE

266
00:23:25,403 --> 00:23:27,155
What do we do, Viktor?

267
00:24:29,009 --> 00:24:31,553
Angelito… Angelito!

268
00:24:33,305 --> 00:24:35,640
Angelito… Angelito, stay with me.

269
00:24:53,700 --> 00:24:55,035
He didn't make it.
